--- 7. why the new text should not go stale the way the old text did ---
The replaced prose asserted a status ('Only the K0 gate is complete', 'has not been built
yet') that silently became wrong when K1.1 was accepted. The new prose is written so its
failure mode is INCOMPLETE rather than FALSE:
  - 'A gate named on a page is the contract for that gate, not a claim that the gate has
    shipped' — a rule, not a status; cannot go stale.
  - '...are implemented under K1.1' — implementation does not un-happen; stays true.
  - '...belong to later gates; the ledger says which of them have since landed' — when K1.2
    lands this sentence becomes less informative, not untrue.
  - Every precise question is delegated to 007 and 002 by name.
This is the same delegation the packet applied to execution-cycle.md, now stated at Layer 1
as a rule, which is what makes it checkable rather than a habit.
